**How to implement.** Every seeded preset gets its frozen GUID, and a new user source is a plain GUID (.spec-md §3.3; 001 §B). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, `PresetIds`: the text of each of the 33 members becomes a GUID minted once while implementing (`[guid]::NewGuid()`), written `ElementValueId "<guid>"` in the lowercase hyphenated form a `Guid`'s `string` prints. No two are equal, and none equals a `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds` or `SampleIds` literal. From this step the literals are frozen: S1.5 exports them byte-for-byte. (2) `newSourceId` (`:592-594`) mints `ElementValueId (string (Guid.NewGuid ()))`; its doc says the id is a plain GUID string, as a sample's is (`SampleId.toElementValueId`, `:43`). (3) `LibraryEntry.entryId`'s doc (`:355-356`) says every entry id is the string of a GUID: a sample's `SampleId`, a preset's `PresetIds` member, a user source's minted id. `liveLibrary` (`:1130-1168`) keeps its code: its `Guid.TryParse` probe (`:1159`) now parses a preset id too, finds no sample (`SampleStore.fs:119` answers `Ok None` for an unknown id) and falls through to the presets. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs` gains `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`: over `liveLibrary (createInMemory ()) samples sources`, with a user source saved under `newSourceId ()` and a sample saved under `newSampleId ()`, `tryGetEntry` returns the ellipsometer detector for `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, the user source for its id and the sample for `toElementValueId` of its id, and `Ok None` for a fresh GUID that names nothing. (5) No product ordering changes. A fact that fails only because it relied on the old ids' alphabetical order compares order-independently, with its assertion otherwise unchanged. Afterwards `git grep -n -E "(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))" -- "Berreman/*.fs"` finds nothing; from S1.4's first step its invariant `s04-no-seeded-string-preset-ids` runs that grep after every step.

**Acceptance.** After the GUIDs are minted, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal` and `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`, which step 19 left red, and `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`; ui-tests over the selected classes MUST pass, including `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id`; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.
